Let  $M$  be a midpoint of  $CD$  and  $O$  be a center of this circle, then  $OM \; \bot \; CD$ . Note that
\[CE^2+DE^2 =(CE+DE)^2 - 2 \cdot CE \cdot DE = CD^2 - 2 \cdot CE \cdot DE\]
