We have  $OE= 5\sqrt{2} - 2\sqrt{5}$ . Because  $\angle OEM=\angle EOM= 45^\circ$ , we have
\[OM = \frac{5\sqrt{2} - 2\sqrt{5}}{\sqrt{2}} = 5- \sqrt{10}\]
With Pythagorean Theorem, then
\begin{align*}
CM^2 &= \left (5\sqrt{2} \right )^2 - \left (5-\sqrt{10}\right )^2
&= 15+10\sqrt{10}
CD^2 &= 60 + 40\sqrt{10}
\end{align*}
From Power Of Point,
\[CE \cdot ED = AE \cdot EB= 2\left (10\sqrt{2} - 2\sqrt{5} \right ) \cdot 2\sqrt{5} = 40 \sqrt{10} - 40\]
And then
\[CE^2 + ED^2 = 60 + 40\sqrt{10} - 40\sqrt{10} + 40 = \boxed{100}\]

