My favorite problem on the test.

Let  $\omega = e^{2i\pi/7}$ . Note that
\begin{align*}
    \cos{\frac{2\pi}7} &= \frac{\omega + \omega^{-1}}{2} 
    \cos{\frac{4\pi}7} &= \frac{\omega^2 + \omega^{-2}}{2} 
    \cos{\frac{6\pi}7} &= \frac{\omega^3 + \omega^{-3}}{2}.
\end{align*}Let these be  $r, s, t$  respectively. By Vieta's formulas, note that the desired quantity is
\begin{align*}
    (-rst)(rs + st + tr)(-r - s - t) = (r + s + t)(rs + st + tr)(rst).
\end{align*}Note that  $1 + \omega + \cdots + \omega^6 = 0$ . We have
\begin{align*}
    r + s + t &= \frac{\omega + \omega^2 + \omega^3 + \omega^{-1} + \omega^{-2} + \omega^{-3}}{2} 
    &= \frac{\omega + \omega^2 + \cdots + \omega^6}{2} 
    &= -\frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}Then,
\begin{align*}
    rs + st + tr &= \frac{\omega^3 + \omega + \omega^{-1} + \omega^{-3}}{4} + \frac{\omega^5 + \omega + \omega^{-1} + \omega^{-5}}{4} + \frac{\omega^4 + \omega^2 + \omega^{-2} + \omega^{-4}}{4} 
    &= \frac{2(\omega + \omega^2 + \cdots + \omega^6)}{4} 
    &= -\frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}Finally,
\begin{align*}
    rst &= \frac{\omega^6 + \omega^4 + \omega^2 + \omega^0 + \omega^0 + \omega^{-2} + \omega^{-4} + \omega^{-6}}{8} 
    &= \frac{(\omega^6 + \omega^5 + \cdots + \omega^0) + \omega^0}{8} 
    &= \frac{1}{8}.
\end{align*}
Multiplying yields the answer of  $\boxed{\textbf{(D) }\frac{1}{32}}$ .

