Set  $d = FV$ , which by the definition of a parabola also equals  $VP$ .  Then as  $AQ = AF = 20$ , we have  $AY = 20 - d$  and  $AX = |20 - 2d|$ .  Since  $FXYV$  is a rectangle,  $FX = VY$ , so by Pythagorean Theorem on triangles  $AFX$  and  $AVY$ ,
\begin{align*}
21^2 - (20 - d)^2 &= AV^2 - AY^2 = VY^2
&= FX^2 = AF^2 - AX^2 = 20^2 - (20 - 2d)^2.
\end{align*}
This equation simplifies to  $3d^2 - 40d + 41 = 0$ , which has solutions  $d = \tfrac{20\pm\sqrt{277}}3$ .  Both values of  $d$  work - the smaller solution with the right configuration and the larger solution with the left configuration - and so the requested answer is  $\boxed{\tfrac{40}3}$ .</details>

