solution_md:
We use Burnside's Lemma. Let  $X$  be the number of two colorings of the nine squares and let  $G = \mathbb{Z}/4\mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z} = \langle r, s \mid r^4 = s^2 = 1\rangle$  act on  $X$ . We want to count the number of orbits, and \[\mathcal{O} = \frac{1}{\left|G\right|}\sum_{g \in G}\left|{\text{FixPt}g}\right|.\]
Now, the following table gives the number of fixed points under each action  $G$ :

\begin{tabular}{|llll|}
\hline $1_G$             &  $r$   &  $r^2$   &  $r^3$     $\binom{9}{2}$  &  $0$   &  $4$     &  $0$      \hline $s$             &  $sr$  &  $sr^2$  &  $sr^3$    $6$             &  $6$   &  $6$     &  $6$      \hline
\end{tabular}


We compute: \[\mathcal{O} = \frac{1}{8}\left(\left|{36}\right|+\left|{0}\right|+\left|{4}\right|+\left|{0}\right|+\left|{6}\right|+\left|{6}\right|+\left|{6}\right|+\left|{6}\right|\right) = \boxed{\text{(C)}\ 8}.\]

