candidates:
Notice that the answer is of the form  $\sqrt{n^4 \sqrt{n^3 \sqrt{n^2}}}$ . We can now look at the graph of \[y = \sqrt{x^4\sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}}\] From the chain rule we have 
\begin{align}
\frac{dy}{dx} \sqrt{x^4\sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}} &= \frac{1}{2\cdot \sqrt{x^4\sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}}} \cdot \frac{dy}{dx} x^4 \sqrt{x^3 \sqrt{x^2}} 
&= \frac{1}{2\cdot \sqrt{x^4\sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}}}\cdot \left( 4x^3 \cdot \sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}} + x^4 \frac{dy}{dx} \sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}} \right)  
&= \frac{1}{2\cdot \sqrt{x^4\sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}}}\cdot \left( 4x^3 \cdot \sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}} + x^4 \left(\frac{1}{2 \cdot \sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}} \cdot \frac{dy}{dx}x^3\sqrt{x^2} \right) \right)  
&= \frac{1}{2\cdot \sqrt{x^4\sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}}}\cdot \left( 4x^3 \cdot \sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}} + x^4 \left(\frac{1}{2 \cdot \sqrt{x^3\sqrt{x^2}}} \cdot 4x^3 \right) \right)  
&= 3x^2
\end{align}

Now we can use the fundamental theorem of calculus to see that our answer is \[\int_0^2 3x^2 = \boxed{8} \]

