[font=futura]<span style="font-size:150%">**<span style="color:#58a1ad">21</span> Problem 21**</span>[/font]
[rule]
A game board consists of  $64$  squares that alternate in color between black and white. The figure below shows square  $P$  in the bottom row and square  $Q$  in the top row. A marker is placed at  $P$ . A *step* consists of moving the marker onto one of the adjoining white squares in the row above. How many  $7$ -step paths are there from  $P$  to  $Q$ ? (The figure shows a sample path.)

[asy]
size(200);
int[] x = {6, 5, 4, 5, 6, 5, 6};
int[] y = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7};
int N = 7;
for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
for (int j = 0; j < 8; ++j) {
draw((i,j)--(i+1,j)--(i+1,j+1)--(i,j+1)--(i,j));
if ((i+j) % 2 == 0) {
filldraw((i,j)--(i+1,j)--(i+1,j+1)--(i,j+1)--(i,j)--cycle,black);
}
}
}
for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
draw(circle((x[i],y[i])+(0.5,0.5),0.35));
}
label(" $P$ ", (5.5, 0.5));
label(" $Q$ ", (6.5, 7.5));
[/asy] $\textbf{(A) }28\qquad \textbf{(B) }30\qquad \textbf{(C) }32\qquad \textbf{(D) }33\qquad \textbf{(E) }35$ [rule]
[font=futura]<span style="font-size:150%">**Solution**</span>[/font]
[rule]
[font=futura]<span style="color:#58a1ad">**Answer (A):**</span>[/font] Note that, for a given spot on the board, the number of ways to get to that spot is equal to the sum of the number of ways to get to the spots diagonally behind it (and these are the only ways to get to that spot). 

Thus, we can label each white square, starting from  $P$  (which we label with  $1$  way) and stopping at  $Q$ ; we will eventually get that the number of  $7$ -step paths from  $P$  to  $Q$  is  $\definecolor{maincolor}{rgb}{0.345098039, 0.631372549, 0.678431373}\color{maincolor}\boxed{\textbf{(A) }28}.$ [asy]
size(200);
int N = 7;
for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
for (int j = 0; j < 8; ++j) {
draw((i,j)--(i+1,j)--(i+1,j+1)--(i,j+1)--(i,j));
if ((i+j) % 2 == 0) {
filldraw((i,j)--(i+1,j)--(i+1,j+1)--(i,j+1)--(i,j)--cycle,black);
}
}
}
label(" $1$ ", (5.5, .5));
label(" $1$ ", (4.5, 1.5));
label(" $1$ ", (6.5, 1.5));
label(" $1$ ", (3.5, 2.5));
label(" $1$ ", (7.5, 2.5));
label(" $2$ ", (5.5, 2.5));
label(" $1$ ", (2.5, 3.5));
label(" $3$ ", (6.5, 3.5));
label(" $3$ ", (4.5, 3.5));
label(" $4$ ", (3.5, 4.5));
label(" $3$ ", (7.5, 4.5));
label(" $6$ ", (5.5, 4.5));
label(" $10$ ", (4.5, 5.5));
label(" $9$ ", (6.5, 5.5));
label(" $19$ ", (5.5, 6.5));
label(" $9$ ", (7.5, 6.5));
label(" $28$ ", (6.5, 7.5));
[/asy] $\definecolor{maincolor}{rgb}{0.345098039, 0.631372549, 0.678431373}\color{maincolor}\blacksquare$ [rule]

