[font=futura]<span style="font-size:150%">**<span style="color:#58a1ad">24</span> Problem 24**</span>[/font]
[rule]
A large square region is paved with  $n^2$  gray square tiles, each measuring  $s$  inches on a side. A border  $d$  inches wide surrounds each tile. The figure below shows the case for  $n=3$ . When  $n=24$ , the  $576$  gray tiles cover  $64\%$  of the area of the large square region. What is the ratio  $\frac{d}{s}$  for this larger value of  $n$ ?

[asy]
    size(150);
draw((0,0)--(13,0)--(13,13)--(0,13)--cycle);
filldraw((1,1)--(4,1)--(4,4)--(1,4)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((1,5)--(4,5)--(4,8)--(1,8)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((1,9)--(4,9)--(4,12)--(1,12)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((5,1)--(8,1)--(8,4)--(5,4)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((5,5)--(8,5)--(8,8)--(5,8)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((5,9)--(8,9)--(8,12)--(5,12)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((9,1)--(12,1)--(12,4)--(9,4)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((9,5)--(12,5)--(12,8)--(9,8)--cycle, mediumgray);
filldraw((9,9)--(12,9)--(12,12)--(9,12)--cycle, mediumgray);
[/asy] $\textbf{(A) }\dfrac{6}{25}\qquad\textbf{(B) }\dfrac{1}{4}\qquad\textbf{(C) }\dfrac{9}{25}\qquad\textbf{(D) }\dfrac{7}{16}\qquad\textbf{(E) }\dfrac{9}{16}$ [rule]
[font=futura]<span style="font-size:150%">**Solution**</span>[/font]
[rule]
[font=futura]<span style="color:#58a1ad">**Answer (A):**</span>[/font] Note that  $s$  and  $d$  are directly proportional, so we can let  $s=1$ . Then. the area of the  $576$  gray tiles is equal to  $576 \cdot 1 \cdot 1 = 576$  square inches, which covers  $64\%$  of the area of the large square region. Thus, the area of the large square region is equal to   $$ \dfrac{576}{64\%}=900 $$   square inches, and so the side length of the large square region is  $\sqrt{900}=30$ . 

We see that, on a given side length of the large square region, there are  $25$  lengths that are  $d$  inches wide surrounding the  $24$  sides of length  $s$ , so the side length of the large square region is equal to  $24+25d$ . 

As well, since the side length of the large square region is equal to  $30$ , we can set the two values equal, which gives
\begin{align*}
    24+25d&=30
    (24+25d)-24&=30-24
    25d&=6
    \dfrac{25d}{25}&=\dfrac{6}{25}
    d&=\dfrac{6}{25}.
    \end{align*}
    Thus, since  $s = 1$ , we get that  $\dfrac{d}{s}=\dfrac{d}{1}=d=\definecolor{maincolor}{rgb}{0.345098039, 0.631372549, 0.678431373}\color{maincolor}\boxed{\textbf{(A) }\dfrac{6}{25}}.$   $\definecolor{maincolor}{rgb}{0.345098039, 0.631372549, 0.678431373}\color{maincolor}\blacksquare$ [rule]

