First, note that the average velocity will be given as 
\[v_{\text{avg}} = \frac{d_{\text{total}}}{t_{\text{total}}}.\]
In order to think of this  in terms of area, we note that the total distance that both Naomi and Maya travelled in the end is the same and that  $v_{\text{avg}}\propto 1/t$ . Three of Naomi's "rectangles" make up Maya's "rectangle" which means that the difference between both is  $2/3$  of the total area of the graph. Naomi's average velocity is  $6/(1/6) = 36$  which means the difference in average velocities will be  $36\cdot (2/3) = 24$ . 

