Upon inspection, notice that  $PT\parallel QR$ , so  $\angle QRU = 45^{\circ}.$  Thus,  $QR = PT = h\sqrt{2} $  and  $RU = h,$  by  $45-45-90$  triangle relations. Again, by  $45-45-90$  triangles,  $PS = 8\sqrt{2},$  so  $TS = TR = 8\sqrt{2}-h\sqrt{2}.$  The area of rectangle  $PQRT$  is then  $h\sqrt{2}\cdot (8\sqrt{2}-h\sqrt{2}).$  The area of  $\triangle RST$  is equal to  $\frac{1}{2}\cdot (8\sqrt{2}-h\sqrt{2})^2.$ By  $45-45-90$  triangle relations and symmetry,  $RZ = 2RY = 2\cdot 12 = 24,$  so the area of  $\triangle XRZ = \frac{1}{2}\cdot 12\cdot 24 = 144.$  Since the total area of the shaded region is  $183$ , we have
\begin{align*}
 h\sqrt{2}\cdot (8\sqrt{2}-h\sqrt{2}) + \frac{1}{2}\cdot (8\sqrt{2}-h\sqrt{2})^2 + 144 &= 183   
 16h - 2h^2 + \frac{1}{2}\cdot \left(\sqrt{2}^2\cdot\left(8-h\right)^2 \right) &= 39 
 16h-2h^2 + 64-16h + h^2 &=39
 25&=h^2,
\end{align*}
so  $h = \boxed{\textbf{(B)\ 5}}.$</details>

